finance reform, but we will never even get that&nbsp;
opportunity if everybody on the left is like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:26.960
I won't even do campaign donations. Now, the&nbsp;
person who raises more money tends to win. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:34.080
it's just an unfortunate reality. Let's go next to&nbsp;
let's go to Browdy from Dallas. We haven't heard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:39.920
from Brody for a while. What's going on there?
Speaker 3: Hey, what's up, David? I'm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:43.120
doing pretty well, how are you?
Speaker 1: I'm doing well, thank you.&nbsp;

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:49.280
Speaker 3: Thanks. I wasn't expecting you to call&nbsp;
me so quickly. It's good to speak to you again. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:53.360
had a few questions regarding the&nbsp;
infrastructure bill and the midterms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.720 --> 00:04:00.240
